# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  Media node — ComfyUI + FastAPI adapter
#
#  Serves three modalities from one ComfyUI on a single GB10 (SM121):
#    av     MiniMax-H3             video with native stereo audio
#    music  ACE-Step 1.5 XL Turbo  text-to-music
#    image  Qwen-Image-2.1       text-to-image at 2048px
#
#  Unlike Dockerfile.comfyui — which pins pytorch:25.01 and has no SM121
#  kernels, hence its ~12s/step — this builds on CUDA 13 and installs PyTorch
#  from PyPI, whose aarch64 wheels are CUDA 13 builds. Those ship sm_120 cubins,
#  which run on the GB10's sm_121 by CUDA's forward compatibility within a major
#  compute capability (verified: bf16/fp16/int8 kernels all execute).
#
#  Build:  docker build -f Dockerfile.media -t media-node:latest .
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

FROM nvidia/cuda:13.0.3-cudnn-runtime-ubuntu24.04

ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive \
    PIP_BREAK_SYSTEM_PACKAGES=1 \
    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1

RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        python3 python3-pip python3-venv \
        git ffmpeg \
        libgl1 libglib2.0-0 \
        curl ca-certificates \
        # Triton JIT-compiles kernels at request time (H3's NVFP4 encoder and the
        # int8/convrot ops need it) and shells out to cc, linking a launcher stub
        # against Python.h. Without these it fails mid-graph with
        # "Failed to find C compiler" — after the container reports healthy.
        gcc python3-dev \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# PyTorch first, so ComfyUI's requirements.txt finds it already satisfied and
# does not pull a different build. torchaudio is required: comfy_extras/
# nodes_minimax_h3.py imports it for reference-audio resampling.
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir torch torchvision torchaudio

# ComfyUI — H3 landed in Comfy-Org/ComfyUI#15224 (2026-08-03); ACE-Step 1.5 and
# Qwen-Image-2.1 are also native. Pin via ARG to freeze a known-good commit.
ARG COMFYUI_REF=88ab4a06566454ad89db8f0bedb970d6c08cd1b7
RUN git clone https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI.git /opt/ComfyUI \
    && cd /opt/ComfyUI \
    && git checkout "${COMFYUI_REF}" \
    && pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt

# Adapter dependencies (ComfyUI already brings aiohttp).
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir fastapi "uvicorn[standard]"

# Weights live on the host and are mounted read-only at /models; point ComfyUI's
# loaders at them instead of copying ~110 GB into the image. One entry per model
# family, since each ships a different tree — ACE-Step keeps HuggingFace's
# split_files/ prefix so its download stays resumable in place.
RUN printf '%s\n' \
    'minimax_h3:' \
    '  base_path: /models/minimax-h3' \
    '  diffusion_models: diffusion_models' \
    '  text_encoders: text_encoders' \
    '  vae: vae' \
    'ace_step_15:' \
    '  base_path: /models/ace-step-1.5/split_files' \
    '  diffusion_models: diffusion_models' \
    '  text_encoders: text_encoders' \
    '  vae: vae' \
    'qwen_image_21:' \
    '  base_path: /models/qwen-image-2.1' \
    '  diffusion_models: diffusion_models' \
    '  text_encoders: text_encoders' \
    '  vae: vae' \
    > /opt/ComfyUI/extra_model_paths.yaml

COPY inference/media_server.py /opt/adapter/media_server.py

# ComfyUI UI is published on 8188; the adapter still uses loopback.
ENV COMFY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8188 \
    PORT=8010
EXPOSE 8010 8188

# Two processes: ComfyUI, and the adapter as PID 1. If ComfyUI dies
# the adapter is signalled so the container exits and `restart: unless-stopped`
# brings the pair back together — otherwise the adapter would keep answering
# /health with a permanent boot error.
RUN printf '%s\n' \
    '#!/usr/bin/env bash' \
    'set -euo pipefail' \
    '# exec below preserves this PID, so $$ is the adapter (PID 1 in a container).' \
    'main_pid=$$' \
    'python3 /opt/ComfyUI/main.py --listen 0.0.0.0 --port 8188 --disable-auto-launch &' \
    'comfy_pid=$!' \
    '( while kill -0 "$comfy_pid" 2>/dev/null; do sleep 5; done' \
    '  echo "ComfyUI exited — shutting down the adapter" >&2' \
    '  kill -TERM "$main_pid" ) &' \
    'exec python3 -m uvicorn media_server:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port "${PORT}" --app-dir /opt/adapter' \
    > /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh \
    && chmod +x /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh

# start-period must cover COMFY_BOOT_TIMEOUT_S (600s by default), because
# /health answers 503 for the whole boot. Any shorter and the container flips to
# unhealthy while it is still legitimately loading ~63 GB of weights. Raise both
# together if a family gets slower to load.
HEALTHCHECK --interval=15s --timeout=10s --start-period=660s --retries=3 \
    CMD curl -fsS http://localhost:8010/health || exit 1

ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh"]
